# Industry Research
Research Item 001

Source Type:
Industry Research

Source:
NNG

Topic:
License Discovery

Observation:
Users perform better when interfaces support recognition rather than recall. Information should be visible and recognizable instead of requiring users to remember identifiers, codes, or navigation paths.

Translation to License Management:
Users should recognize product names rather than remember entitlement IDs, contract numbers, or SKUs.

Examples:
- Microsoft 365 Business Premium
- VMware vSphere
- Dell APEX Backup Services

Key takeaway:
Use product names as the primary discovery mechanism for software licenses.

Confidence:
High

Sources:
https://www.nngroup.com/articles/recognition-and-recall/
https://www.nngroup.com/articles/ten-usability-heuristics/

---

Research Item 002

Source Type:
Industry Research

Source:
NNG

Topic:
Terminology

Observation:
Interfaces should use terminology familiar to users rather than internal system terminology or organizational jargon.

Translation to License Management:
Users understand:
- License
- Subscription
- Product
- User

More easily than:
- Entitlement
- Consumption Right
- Provisioning Object
- Service Plan

Key takeaway:
Use customer language rather than entitlement language.

Confidence:
High

Sources:
https://www.nngroup.com/articles/ten-usability-heuristics/

